* EEF1 bicelle (modified parabolic pore) implicit-membrane test
* Validates MR!337 (model: Themis Lazaridis; fixes/integration: J. Buckner).
* Capture-free, self-reports via the testcheck macro:
*   PART 1  analytic first derivatives of the bicelle solvation energy,
*           checked against finite differences by TEST FIRST.  The EEF1
*           solvation term is ISOLATED with "skip all excl asp" so the
*           check is not polluted by finite-difference noise from the
*           cutoff-switched vdw/elec/bonded terms.  Every component must
*           agree: NOK = 3*NATOM.  Probed at several placements spanning
*           the disk interior, the radial edge (RC~1), the exterior, and
*           off the midplane, so the radial (DGDR/DFDR/DRDZ) and axial
*           (DFDZ) derivative paths are all exercised.
*   PART 2  exercises the fixed SLVPRINT (eef1 print) bicelle branch.
*   PART 3  shows rbic+rprb double-applies the pore term (the conflict the
*           mutual-exclusivity guard rejects).
*
if ?aspener .ne. 1 then
   echo "Test NOT performed - ASPENER (EEF1) not compiled."
   stop
endif
if ?numnode .ne. 1 then
   echo "Test NOT performed in parallel."
   stop
endif

stream datadir.def

open read card unit 3 name @0toph19_eef1.1.inp
read rtf unit 3 card
close unit 3
open read card unit 3 name @0param19_eef1.1.inp
read para unit 3 card
close unit 3
open read unit 3 card name @0testimm1.crd
read seque coor unit 3
close unit 3
generate main setup
open read unit 2 card name @0testimm1.crd
read coor card unit 2
close unit 2

set rbic = 40.0
set tolabs = -0.5      ! negative => absolute; NOK must equal the DOF count
calc ndof = 3 * ?natom

! ===================== PART 1 : derivatives =====================
! nsmp 29 is the physically-appropriate radial smoothness for a 40-Ang
! bicelle (T. Lazaridis) -- do NOT lower it to get smoother finite
! differences; a small nsmp is a bad model.  The derivative check stays
! valid because it isolates the EEF1 solvation term (skip all excl asp)
! and uses a small finite-difference step.
eef1 setup membrane slvt water slv2 chex nsmth 10 width 30.0 temp 298.15 -
     unit 93 name @0solvpar.inp aemp 0.85 rbic @rbic aprb 10.0 nsmp 29
update ctonnb 7. ctofnb 9. cutnb 10. group rdie
skip all excl asp

! radial edge (center ~ RBIC), at the midplane
coor orient
coor trans xdir @rbic ydir 0.0 zdir 0.0
update
energy
test first step 0.00001 tol 0.001 sele all end
@testcheck ?nok @ndof @tolabs EEF1_BIC_DERIV_EDGE_MID

! radial edge, off the midplane (exercises DRDZ + RPOR(z))
coor orient
coor trans xdir @rbic ydir 0.0 zdir 12.0
update
energy
test first step 0.00001 tol 0.001 sele all end
@testcheck ?nok @ndof @tolabs EEF1_BIC_DERIV_EDGE_OFFMID

! interior of the disk (small radius)
coor orient
coor trans xdir 8.0 ydir 0.0 zdir 4.0
update
energy
test first step 0.00001 tol 0.001 sele all end
@testcheck ?nok @ndof @tolabs EEF1_BIC_DERIV_INSIDE

! exterior of the disk (large radius)
coor orient
coor trans xdir 70.0 ydir 0.0 zdir 4.0
update
energy
test first step 0.00001 tol 0.001 sele all end
@testcheck ?nok @ndof @tolabs EEF1_BIC_DERIV_OUTSIDE

skip none

! ===================== PART 2 : slvprint fix =====================
! Pre-fix the per-atom loop used RPOR = RPRB - APRB*z'^2 (negative for
! rbic-only) -> divergent per-atom report.  SLVPRINT's per-atom values
! are not queryable, so we exercise the fixed branch and confirm it
! leaves the (correct) total energy unchanged.  The per-atom math itself
! is validated by PART 1 (same RPOR = RBIC - APRB*z'^2 formula).
coor orient
coor trans xdir @rbic ydir 0.0 zdir 6.0
update
energy
set eref = ?ener
eef1 print
energy
calc dprint = abs ( ?ener - @eref )
@testcheck @dprint 0.0 -0.001 EEF1_BIC_SLVPRINT_CONSISTENT

! ===================== PART 3 : rbic/rprb conflict =====================
! At default bomlev the guard makes rbic+rprb fatal.  Here we lower
! bomlev so the WRNDIE(-2) is survivable and show the combination
! double-applies the pore term (energy differs from rbic-only) - the
! very conflict the guard rejects.
set ebic = ?ener
bomlev -5
eef1 setup membrane slvt water slv2 chex nsmth 10 width 30.0 temp 298.15 -
     unit 93 name @0solvpar.inp aemp 0.85 rbic @rbic rprb @rbic aprb 10.0 nsmp 29
bomlev 0
update
energy
set eboth = ?ener
calc ddbl = abs ( @eboth - @ebic )
if @ddbl .gt. 0.01 then
   set teststat pass
else
   set teststat fail
   incr testfail by 1
endif
echo EEF1_BIC_RBIC_RPRB_CONFLICT testcase result: @teststat

echo ============================================================
echo   EEF1 bicelle test complete : @testfail failure(s)
echo ============================================================
stop
